<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bhangani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1688</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bhangani was fought in 1688 near Paonta Sahib in the Himalayan foothills between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guru-gobind-singh">Guru Gobind Singh</a> and the forces of Raja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fateh-shah-of-garhwal">Fateh Shah of Garhwal</a> and his allies among the hill rajas. It was the Guru's first battle, and his own account of it in the Bachittar Natak describes a victory. Afterwards he left Paonta and returned to Anandpur.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bhangani.jpg" alt="Battle of Bhangani" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Painting_of_Guru_Gobind_Singh_mounted_up_for_a_battle_atop_of_an_elephant,_circa_late_17th_to_early_18th_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
